This code implements a scalable C application that integrates asynchronous DNS resolution and efficient file processing functionalities. The program handles a high volume of concurrent DNS requests and processes large text files containing comma-separated data. Asynchronous DNS resolution is implemented using a non-blocking resolver to minimize latency and handle potential delays and timeouts robustly. The resolved IP addresses are stored in a thread-safe cache to support concurrent lookups, ensuring thread safety and efficient memory management. The file processing module reads and parses each line, calculating the average of the last two numerical fields while gracefully handling lines with varying lengths and missing fields by providing default values when necessary. Memory usage for storing DNS results and file lines is optimized to prevent leaks and ensure optimal performance under heavy load. A reliable file upload library is used to handle uploads from URLs, returning the URL of the uploaded file upon successful completion. The application is designed with modularity in mind to facilitate future enhancements, allowing seamless integration of additional features such as logging, monitoring, and performance optimizations. The balance between resource allocation for DNS resolution and file processing is ensured by using a non-blocking resolver for DNS resolution and efficient memory management techniques for storing DNS results and file lines. A robust error-handling mechanism and detailed logging are implemented to aid in debugging and maintenance.']

