Supporting different serialization formats has trade-offs between maintainability and performance. While supporting new features may introduce complexity, it also allows for better data compatibility and interoperability with other systems. However, maintaining backward compatibility can also be challenging, requiring significant code modifications to ensure that existing data remains compatible with the new format.

