The `Task` class represents a unit of work that can be executed by the thread pool manager. It has a runnable function that is executed when the task is picked up by a worker thread. The task also has a priority level, which can be used to prioritize tasks based on user-defined criteria.

The `Future` class represents the result of an asynchronous task. It provides a way to wait for the task to complete and get its status.

The `ConcurrencyUtils` class provides a simple interface for submitting tasks, getting their status, and stopping the thread pool manager. The thread pool manager dynamically adjusts its size based on system load metrics, CPU usage, and queue length. It also implements a sophisticated scheduling strategy that prioritizes tasks based on user-defined priority levels and ensures that each task is logged with timestamps upon submission, completion, and failure.

