This code block implements the `processUserRequest` function that manages user account operations for an online platform. The function accepts a `$_POST` array containing the keys `id` (optional), `name`, `email`, `password`, `sub_action`, and `locale`. It performs actions based on the value of the `sub_action` key, which can be either `create`, `update`, `delete`, or `list`. The function handles JSON responses appropriately and ensures that the `id` is present when performing read, update, or delete operations. It validates required fields (`name`, `email`, `password`) and enforces a constraint that no two users can have the same email address within the specified `locale`. It uses separate methods for each operation to ensure modularity and maintainability. The function also handles performance implications when handling large datasets and implements pagination within the `List` method to support up to 100 users per page with a default limit of 50. It optimizes repeated read operations using caching mechanisms, but design cache invalidation strategies carefully to prevent outdated data from being served to users. The function supports internationalization by handling different locales and ensuring that all text returned in JSON responses is locale-aware.

