The code uses a semaphore to control concurrency, ensuring thread safety and preventing race conditions. It also optimizes memory usage by only loading necessary parts of the file into memory for parsing.

To log processed files, the code maintains a log of start and end times as well as any errors encountered during processing. The logging frequency is balanced between performance and log size to minimize overhead while still providing useful information.

The code also supports integration with an external service via HTTP POST request, allowing for proper handling of API rate limits and retries in case of failures. The impact of this integration on overall system latency and reliability is evaluated, and appropriate measures are taken to mitigate any negative effects.

Overall, the code is designed to be robust, scalable, and maintain high performance under various loads while balancing efficiency, usability, maintainability, and scalability."]

