The system is designed to handle dynamic scaling, adapting to varying workloads and resource constraints. It also includes a mechanism for efficient memory reclamation, ensuring that resources are released promptly when no longer needed while minimizing impact on system performance.

Finally, the code is modular and easily extendable, allowing for future enhancements or modifications without extensive refactoring.']

