This is the final version of the logging system that I implemented. It has all the features I mentioned earlier, including multi-level logging, buffering, and asynchronous flushing. The `initializeLogging()` function initializes the logging system with default values for various parameters such as log file path, rotation size, and buffer size. The `log()` function formats a log message using the given format string and arguments, and then appends it to the log buffer. If the buffer is full or the maximum memory usage limit has been reached, it flushes the buffer to the log file and creates a new one with doubled capacity. The `parseArguments()` function parses the command line arguments and updates the logging system accordingly. The `main()` function sets up the signal handler for SIGINT and calls `initializeLogging()`.']

