The code block also includes mechanisms to monitor and log errors or warnings for each session, ensuring robustness under high-load conditions. It integrates cryptographic primitives like AES and Camellia block ciphers, MD5 and SHA digests, and RSA with SHA1, leveraging OpenSSL's EVP_add_cipher and EVP_add_digest functions, along with appropriate aliases. Cryptographic functions are optimized for performance to handle large-scale load testing and stress scenarios without degradation.

